    <outcome date="2026-10-02" branch="task/uac-r2-157-b2-r1" round="review-4-fix-b2-r1" base="a2d6ffd48">
      Status stays "completed-with-escalation". Two items stay open: the MANUAL live gate (criterion 6, pending by
      design; deploy order unchanged, note section 5) and the owner decision on F1 (note section 8).
      BLOCKING item 1 (criterion 1; Q1-Q5 compiled into live picker-on mounts and the guard passed them): CLOSED,
      with one documented residual. Before any change, the 5 verifier shapes plus 3 of mine were re-seeded and wired
      into main.tsx. vite build compiled all 8 into a live mount (Q1-Q5 and Q7 onto the shared grid; Q6 onto a SECOND
      instance of the grid module; Q8 onto the shared grid). The guard stayed 81/81 green.
      - Q1/Q2 (the wrapper called as a plain function): outside the wrapper, every import of the wrapper module, by any
        path-like spelling (./, ../, @/, /src/, with or without a script extension, any letter case), binds names that
        may appear only as a JSX tag, after typeof, or as a member name. This is the verifier's fix (a). In such a
        file, cloneElement, createElement and \u are refused. A namespace import, a re-export, an unattributed import
        (string-named or side-effect) and a dynamic import()/require() of the wrapper module are refused too.
        GridWidgetBody.tsx needed comment-only rewording: its JSDoc named the wrapper three times outside a tag, and
        comments are scanned as code.
      - Q3/Q4 (a carrier beside src/, or in a __* / test path): this is the verifier's fix (b). A specifier that names
        the shared library must resolve into the library's src, directly or through the npm link. It may not resolve
        into a __* segment or a .test/.spec/.stories file, with or without the extension. The fan-in fact also gained
        a rule (SharedEscapes): every shipped library file, the allowed carriers included, is refused if it loads a
        module outside src/ or from a test / __* path. Without it, a shipped file could re-export a __* carrier past
        both checks. Q4 class: the fan-in's test exclusion is now sound, because nothing shipped can reach a test path.
      - Q5 (@spaarke/ui-components/../...): this is the verifier's fix (c). The alias is now resolved to the
        library's src, then checked by the same rule. It is no longer trusted by prefix.
      - Q6 (found here): import Table from '@spaarke/ui-components/components/DataGrid/DataGrid?v=1'. Vite loads a
        second module instance, and the default-export rule read the last segment 'DataGrid?v=1' as a non-grid name.
